  "slug": "metabolic-trait-robustness-microbial-e869",
  "summary": "Four database updates extend curated quantitative data on enzyme stability, kinetics and yeast transcription regulation, with new access and curation frameworks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is data infrastructure for enzyme function and metabolic engineering. OrganiZymeDB compiles 28,121 manually curated stability and function measurements in organic solvents from 646 publications. ThermoMutDB 2.0 uses a semiautomated LLM-plus-rule framework to add 1763 thermostability mutation entries with mutant structural models. SABIO-RK has been rebuilt around a unified JSON curation framework, with 60+ field search and a RESTful API returning JSON, CSV, SBML or EnzymeML. YEASTRACT+ adds quantitative TF-target regulation data for 13 yeasts, plus TF-ranking and TF-informed metabolic engineering tools. What is new is the emphasis on quantitative records, structural enrichment, partly automated curation and standardized export. The items are heterogeneous: three concern enzyme biochemistry and one concerns transcriptional regulation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
